 Mouse-wheel scrolling is enabled by default; set a custom pager to override this.
 After the pager exits, the complete rendered document is printed to standard output
 so it remains in terminal scrollback, including when the pager is quit early.
+
+When viewing one regular file interactively with `less`, mdcat saves the top visible
+rendered line on `q` or Ctrl+C and restores it on the next paginated view.
+Positions are stored in `history.toml` next to `config.toml`, keyed by a SHA-256 hash
+of the canonical absolute input filename. Unpaginated views, stdin, combined
+multi-file views, and other pagers do not update this history. The position is a
+rendered line number; edits or changes to wrapping can shift the corresponding text.
+Delete an entry (or `history.toml`) to reset saved positions.
 
